switch WinTag
case 'fdtool_main'
   switch ObjTag
   case {'fdtool_main'}
      Name='Fdident GUI';
      LongHelp=sprintf( ...
         [ ...
            '!@!Identification in General!@!\n' ...
            'In this toolbox we identify a transfer function model of a system, \n' ...
            'starting from measured input-output data. The data can be collected in \n' ...
            'time or in frequency domain. The model can be discrete- or \n' ...
            'continuous-time. Tools are provided to select the best model and to \n' ...
            'calculate uncertainty bounds on the identified model (transfer function, \n' ...
            'poles and zeros, or model parameters). The presence of nonlinear \n' ...
            'distortions can also be detected.\n' ...
            '!@!About the GUI!@!\n' ...
            'The Graphical User Interface for frequency domain system identification is \n' ...
            'based on a flow graph. Blocks represent actions, and arrows represent \n' ...
            'data. A double-click or a right-button mouse click opens the desired \n' ...
            'object. This is true in general for the whole GUI: double-click on many \n' ...
            'objects will open them, or zoom-in, or bring up additional information.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'The states of the individual elements are color-coded (see Colors). Some \n' ...
            'blocks only become selectable when data appear on their input.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'When an inadequate setting is detected, the interface gracefully returns \n' ...
            'for correction with a warning or an error message. The only situation it \n' ...
            'cannot cope with occurs when during execution of an action, the mouse \n' ...
            'selects another control, which starts a parallel action. Therefore, start \n' ...
            'a new action only when the previous one is done (see the status line at \n' ...
            'the bottom of the main window).\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'In most cases the user is prevented from too early actions by making the \n' ...
            'marker inactive (hourglass-form). However, parallel execution can cause \n' ...
            'such possibilities on certain platforms. When this happens, the marker may \n' ...
            'remain inactive. In such a case move the cursor a little bit over a \n' ...
            'window. This will allow again the continuation of the work. If this does \n' ...
            'not help, select "File" / "Unfreeze GUI" in the main window.\n' ...
            '!@!Different User Levels!@!\n' ...
            'Uitoggletools can set "UserLevel", and by this, modify the complexity of \n' ...
            'the GUI. At this moment "Automatic", and "Interactive" levels are \n' ...
            'available.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'At level "Automatic", a number of default settings and automatic \n' ...
            'processing steps are made. This includes automatic data preprocessing and \n' ...
            'automatic order selection (see the help of the block "Estimate Plant \n' ...
            'Model", when you already have preprocessed data at its input).\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'At level "Intermediate", settings can be set manually. Moreover, at \n' ...
            'intermediate level excitation signals can be designed, and complex aspects \n' ...
            'of the models can be viewed.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            '!@!Colors!@!\n' ...
            'Meaning of colors on the main block diagram:\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            '- gray means disabled block or empty arrow (a gray block cannot be opened \n' ...
            'because of lack of input data or too low UserLevel setting),\n' ...
            '- blue means an enabled block (it can be opened) which has not yet been \n' ...
