            '!@!Preparing time domain object!@!\n' ...
            'Here an example is given how to prepare a proper tiddata object for \n' ...
            'importing into the GUI, if the "Compose" window is not used.\n' ...
            'Let us assume that we have measured 4096 time domain samples, which are \n' ...
            'stored in the vectors ''inp'' and ''outp''. The sampling frequency is fs = \n' ...
            '40960 Hz, the period length in each signal is Tp = 1/80 s (there are 8 \n' ...
            'periods). The frequency content is fv = [1:2:15]/Tp.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            '%%Make the object:\n' ...
            'obj = tiddata(outp,inp,1/40960);\n' ...
            '%%Set some properties:\n' ...
            'obj.periodlength = 1/80;\n' ...
            'obj.frequencies = [1:2:15]/80;\n' ...
            'get(obj) %%check properties\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'Now the variable obj can be imported to the block "Read Time Domain \n' ...
            'Data".\n' ...
            '!@! Preparing time domain object, 5 exp!@!\n' ...
            'Here an example is given how to prepare a proper tiddata object from \n' ...
            'multiple experiments for loading into the GUI, if the "Compose" window is \n' ...
            'not used.\n' ...
            'Assume that we have multiple experiments, and let us assume that we have \n' ...
            'measured five times 1024 time domain samples, which are stored in the 1024 \n' ...
            'x 5 arrays inp and outp. The sampling frequency is fs = 40960 Hz, the \n' ...
            'period length in each signal is 1/160 s (there are 4 periods in each \n' ...
            'record).\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            '%%First prepare the data in 1 x 5 cell arrays:\n' ...
            'u = num2cell(inp,1); y = num2cell(outp,1);\n' ...
            '%%Now make the object:\n' ...
            'obj = tiddata(y,u,1/40960);\n' ...
            '%%Set some properties:\n' ...
            'obj.periodlength = 1/160;\n' ...
            'obj.frequencies = [1:2:25]/160;\n' ...
            'obj.synchronization=''on'';\n' ...
            'get(obj) %%check properties\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'Now the variable obj can be imported to the block "Read Time Domain \n' ...
