            '!@! Preparing object from FRF data!@!\n' ...
            'FRF data can be best processed in the "Compose" window, or some more hints \n' ...
            'can be read on the WEB, at \n' ...
            'http://elecwww.vub.ac.be/fdident/frf-data.html\n' ...
            'Here is an example how to prepare a proper fiddata object for loading into \n' ...
            'the GUI, if the "Compose" window is not used.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'Let us assume that we have measured gain and phase data at frequency \n' ...
            'points [100 Hz - 40 kHz], at 50 Hz steps. The gain data are in dB, the \n' ...
            'phase data are in degrees.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'The frequency vector is\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            '     freqv = [100/50:40e3/50]''*50; %%assure proper number of points\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'Now size(freqv), size(gain) and size(phase) should be in general the same, \n' ...
            'all column vectors.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            '     FRF = 10.^(gain/20).*exp(j*phase/360*2*pi);\n' ...
            '     obj = fiddata(FRF,ones(size(FRF)),freqv);\n' ...
