            'elements.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'Now the variable obj can be imported into the block "Read Frequency Domain \n' ...
            'Data".\n' ...
            '!@!Saving models!@!\n' ...
            'The end results can be saved either by selecting the File/Save menu of any \n' ...
            'of the last three blocks, or by double-clicking on an arrow containing a \n' ...
            'model or a set of models. Remark: model saving is not accessible in trial \n' ...
            'versions, but otherwise the toolbox is fully functional for trial.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'The saved variable is a fidmodel object. Its properties contain all \n' ...
            'important information about the model. If the name of the variable is \n' ...
