            'window, "Evaluate or Compare Plant Models".\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'If you have your data at vectors/arrays in the workspace, use the \n' ...
            '"Compose" button: this allows to automatically assemble your data object \n' ...
            'from common Matlab variables in the workspace. If you have your data in \n' ...
            'files, load them first into the workspace, and then execute "Compose". FRF \n' ...
            'data can also be processed in the "Compose" window, or some more hints can \n' ...
            'be read on the WEB, at \n' ...
            'http://elecwww.vub.ac.be/fdident/frf-data.html\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'A last possibility is to make your fiddata object in the command window, \n' ...
            'using the functions ''fiddata''.\n' ...
            '!@!Using Time Domain Data!@!\n' ...
            'Example: open "Read Time Domain Data", and import data with the choices \n' ...
            '"Get Data", "From File", "Browse demos", "robotarm.mat", variable \n' ...
            '"robotarm_rawdata". If you have left "UserLevel" set to "Automatic" in the \n' ...
            'menu of the main window, this block will now automatically preprocess the \n' ...
