   case {'essd_uic_stsgrb(3)'}
      Name='PRBS';
      LongHelp=sprintf( ...
         [ ...
            'A Pseudo Random Binary Sequence (Maximum Length Binary Sequence) is a \n' ...
            'binary signal with almost white spectrum. Its length is 2^M-1 where M is \n' ...
            'an integer.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'When "Odd frequencies" are selected, the algorithm designs a so-called \n' ...
            'inverse repeat sequence in which all even harmonics are set to zero.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'For details in setting the design parameters, see the Help / Help on \n' ...
            'Object applied to the buttons "Adjust freqs" and "Adjust samples".\n' ...
         ]);
      ShortHelp='';
      return
   case {'essd_uic_recfilttext'}
      Name='Smoothing filter';
      LongHelp=sprintf( ...
         [ ...
            'Signal samples are usually led to a digital-analog converter (DAC). Then \n' ...
            'the signal is staircase-like (ZOH). It can be applied to the device under \n' ...
            'test as it is (keeping the signal amplitude constant between the samples), \n' ...
            'or through a smoothing filter (lowpass filter), in order to make the \n' ...
            'signal continuous in amplitude, without modifying the low frequency \n' ...
            'spectral content.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'The application of the DAC (the zero-order hold, ZOH) slightly modifies \n' ...
            'the spectral content in both cases, therefore spectral precompensation is \n' ...
            'applied for the design to provide the desired spectral lines at the output \n' ...
            'of the DAC.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'For discrete intercal signals (DIBS, DITS, MLBS) the smoothing filter does \n' ...
            'not play a role in signal design, its effect is only used in the amplitude \n' ...
            'setting of the generated signal.\n' ...
         ]);
      ShortHelp='';
