            '\n' ...
            'The built-in "generators" correspond to the possible ways of generating an \n' ...
            'analog signal from the discrete sample sequence.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            '"DAC"\n' ...
            'The samples are led to a DAC. The design needs inverse ZOH precompensation \n' ...
            'of the amplitudes. No overshoot is assumed between samples.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            '"Filtered DAC"\n' ...
            'The signal is led to a DAC, then an analog lowpass filter is applied. The \n' ...
            'design needs inverse ZOH precompensation of the amplitudes. Overshoot is \n' ...
            'considered between samples, so this needs to be considered.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            '"Interpolator"\n' ...
            'The discrete samples will be interpolated by bandlimited interpolation. \n' ...
            'The design considers the maximum amplitude of the continuous-time signal. \n' ...
            'This possibility (sample interpolation) is available for multisine design \n' ...
            'only, and only for this "generator".\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            '"Discrete Seq."\n' ...
            'The signal (the discrete sequence) is designed for a discrete system. No \n' ...
            'continuous reconstruction is assumed.\n' ...
         ]);
      ShortHelp='';
      return
