   case {'gfdd_uic_importpb'}
      Name='Import';
      LongHelp=sprintf( ...
         [ ...
            '!@!Import data!@!\n' ...
            'Read fiddata object from workspace, or from file.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'The reading procedure checks the type of the data: they must be "fiddata" \n' ...
            'objects. Such objects can be created by the function "fiddata" from your \n' ...
            'own vectors - see "Help / Getting Started... / Using Freq. Domain Data", and \n' ...
            'the corresponding function helps for details. The objects allow the use of \n' ...
            'the "get" and "set" functions: e.g. get(dat). In frequency domain, don''t \n' ...
            'forget to fill in the "Synchronization" property, e.g. \n' ...
            '\n' ...
            '     data.synchronization=''on'';\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'otherwise unnecessarily long processing time may be necessary later, \n' ...
            'during the execution of the "Variance Analysis" block. If data of more \n' ...
            'than one experiments are used, and measurements are properly synchronized, \n' ...
            'also set the property "synchronization".\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            '!@!Sample program for preparing load!@!\n' ...
            'Let us assume that we have measured five times the input and output \n' ...
            'amplitudes at 25 frequencies. The data are stored in the 25 x 5 arrays inp \n' ...
            'and outp. The frequency vector is freqv.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            '%%First prepare the data in 1 x 5 cell arrays:\n' ...
            'U = num2cell(inp,1); Y = num2cell(outp,1);\n' ...
            '%%Now make the object:\n' ...
            'obj = fiddata(Y,U,freqv);\n' ...
            '%%Set some properties:\n' ...
            'obj.periodlength = 1/160;\n' ...
            'obj.synchronization=''on'';\n' ...
            'get(obj) %%check properties\n' ...
            '\n' ...
            'Now the variable obj can be imported to this block.\n' ...
            '\n' ...
         ]);
